### A book's own accessibility information (EPUB Accessibility metadata).

## Said after the document overview and printed by tw info for an EPUB,
## one fact per line, meaning first. The first line is one of the four
## leads; the details follow when the book gives them. $list is a list of
## terms in words ("table of contents, alternative text"), $text the
## publisher's own words, $name a certifier's name.
access-info-friendly = Accesibilidad: apto para lector de pantalla, según la editorial.
access-info-not-text = Accesibilidad: no todo se lee como texto, según la editorial.
access-info-given = Accesibilidad: descrita por la editorial.
access-info-none = No hay información de accesibilidad.
access-info-summary = Resumen: { $text }.
access-info-modes = Modos de acceso: { $list }.
access-info-sufficient = Se lee con: { $list }.
access-info-features = Funciones: { $list }.
access-info-hazards = Riesgos: { $list }.
access-info-conformance = Cumple: { $text }.
access-info-certifier = Certificado por: { $name }.
# Joins two sets of access modes in access-info-sufficient: "text, or text and images".
access-info-or = { $first }, o { $second }
# Joins the access modes inside one set: "text and images".
access-info-and = { $first } y { $second }
